    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm seeing a CrashLoopBackOff on our auth-service in the prod gke cluster. i checked the logs but it's mostly just restarting. here is the snippet from the event log:\n\n`Back-off restarting failed container`\n`Warning FailedPostStartHook  pod/auth-service-7f8db 10/10/23 14:02:01: failed to run postStart hook: handler was unable to execute: error running postStart hook: exec: \"curl\": executable file not found in $PATH`\n\ncan u give me a checklist of what to check to see if this is a config issue or something else? im kinda stuck.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This error clearly points to an issue with your container image build, not necessarily a runtime config issue. Since the `curl` executable is missing from the container's `$PATH`, your container cannot complete its startup process defined in the pod spec. First, verify your `Dockerfile` to ensure it includes a package manager (like `apt` or `apk`) and explicitly installs common utilities like `curl`. Next, rebuild and push the updated image, and finally, apply the new image tag to your deployment to force a restart.",
      "source": "target",
