    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, that makes sense. we definitely missed curl in the latest slim image build. \n\none thing tho, we also have some other sporadic errors in the cluster where certain pods just die for no obvious reason, no logs, just gone. it's super weird. if it's not a missing binary like this, what else could be causing those \"ghost\" crashes or silent failures in a k8s environment?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Silent or \"ghost\" pod failures often indicate resource exhaustion or underlying node problems rather than application errors. Check your Kubernetes events for `OOMKilled` (Out Of Memory) which is a common cause of sudden termination without application logs. Additionally, monitor the health and resource pressure of the worker nodes themselves, as disk pressure or network issues on the node can cause pods to be evicted abruptly. Finally, review your Quality of Service (QoS) settings to ensure pods aren't being prematurely terminated by the scheduler due to resource contention.",
      "source": "target",
