      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When paranoia sets in, it's often worth investigating control plane and networking layers for subtle issues. Look into Kubernetes admission controllers or webhooks, as a misconfigured security policy or validation could silently block or interfere with pod startup or execution. Also, check for network flapping or misconfigurations in your CNI plugin; intermittent network connectivity loss can cause processes to time out and crash without generating clear application logs. Lastly, investigate any custom resource definitions (CRDs) or operators that might be running, as they sometimes introduce unexpected state management that causes pods to fail subtly.",
